  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 759144,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "## 100 Classic Books: A Portable Literary Treasure\n\nTransform your Nintendo DS into a personal library with *100 Classic Books*, a unique e-book collection developed by Genius Sonority and published by Nintendo. This innovative game, also known as *100 Classic Book Collection*, houses a remarkable selection of one hundred public domain literary works, from Shakespeare’s *Othello* to Dickens’ *Oliver Twist*, all conveniently stored on a single DS cartridge. \n\nExperience the joy of reading in a novel way – hold your DS like a book and customize your reading experience with adjustable text sizes and background music. Features include a bookmark function for easy navigation and a search tool to discover books by genre, author, or length. Delve deeper with author introductions and a fun personality quiz that recommends books tailored to your preferences. \n\nWhile initially released in Europe in December 2008, with subsequent releases in Australia and North America, the game offers a unique blend of classic literature and interactive gameplay, though some critics noted the DS screen size presented a challenge for comfortable reading."
    },
